{
  "info": {
    "title": "Ozone Connect - UAE Insurance API Description",
    "description": "## Ozone Connect - UAE Insurance API Description\n\nThis document provides an API description in [OpenAPI](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.1.html) for Insurance APIs for Ozone Connect.\n\nThese APIs should be implemented by a financial institution to facilitate integration with the API Hub.\n\n### Versioning\n\nThe `version` property implements the following pattern `{standards-major}.{standards-minor}.{ozone-connect-version}`, where:  \n\n* `standards-major` is the major version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n\n* `standards-minor` is the minor version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n\n* `ozone-connect-version` is the version of the Ozone Connect API description.\n\nSo, for example, `v2.0.1` indicates the first version of the Ozone Connect API description that implements the UAE standard version 2.0.\n\n### v2.1.4\n\n* Removed the CAAP-specific header `o3-is-caap-consent-operation` from the `get /{insurance-type}-insurance-policies`\n  operations, the CAAP-conditional `ProductName`, `BodyType`, and `PlateNumber` properties from the insurance\n  policy schemas, and related CAAP-conditional language. CAAP variants of these endpoints have been moved to the\n  CAAP Operations OpenAPI description. `PolicyEndDate` is retained on the insurance policy schemas but is no longer\n  CAAP-conditional: it is now an ordinary optional property, returnable for all consent types, matching the\n  `get /{insurance-type}-insurance-policies` response in the UAE Insurance API description.\n\n\n* Removed the `maximum` of 100 from `AEInsuranceServiceRatingRateOrRatio`, which is referenced by the\n  `ServiceRating` properties `SolvencyRatio`, `ClaimsPaymentCapacityRatio`, `AverageClaimSettlementTime`, and\n  `CustomerComplaintRate`. None of these is a 0-100 percentage: both ratios routinely exceed 100% for a solvent\n  insurer, and the other two are measured in calendar days and in complaints per 1,000 active policies\n  respectively. The two genuine percentages, `ClaimSettlementRatio` and `ClaimRejectionRate`, now reference a new\n  `AEInsuranceServiceRatingPercentage` schema, which retains `maximum: 100` and adds `minimum: 0`.\n\n\n* Changed the `get /{industryType}-insurance-policies/{InsurancePolicyId}` operation to return an optional\n  `CreditDebitIndicator` within `Premium.Adjustments`, indicating whether a premium adjustment is a credit,\n  reducing the premium payable, or a debit, increasing the premium payable. `AdjustmentAmount` is unsigned and\n  carries no direction of its own. Where `CreditDebitIndicator` is absent, the adjustment must be treated as a\n  `Debit`, which is the reading that matches existing v2.1 behaviour.\n\n\n* Removed `format: uuid` from `AEInsurance.AEInsuranceResourceIdentifierType`, the schema behind the\n  `InsurancePolicyId` and `QuoteId` path parameters and the `QuoteId`, `InsurancePolicyId` and related identifier\n  properties. A uuid v4 remains recommended for consistency but is no longer mandatory, so LFIs may use their own\n  identifier scheme within the existing 1-128 character bounds. This matches UAE standards v2.1-errata3.\n\n\n### v2.1.3\n\n\n* Changed the `get /{insurance-type}-insurance-quotes/{QuoteId}` operation to return the correct type for `Pending`\n  `QuoteStatus` responses.\n\n\n### v2.1.2\n\n\n* Changed the `insurancePolicyIds` parameter from optional to mandatory for the `get /{industryType}-insurance-policies` operation.\n\n\n* Changed the guidance for `insurancePolicyIds` parameter for the `get /{industryType}-insurance-policies` operation.\n\n\n### v2.1.1\n\n\n* Initial version that delivers v2.1 requirements (see separate, detailed changelog for changes from last v2.1.x version).\n\n",
    "version": "v2.1.4"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://[Ozone_Connect_API]"
    }
  ],
  "source_path": "/health-insurance-quotes/{QuoteId}",
  "operations": {
    "patch": {
      "operationId": "HealthInsuranceUpdateInsuranceQuoteByQuoteIdOperation",
      "summary": "Accept a health insurance quote",
      "description": "Update the quote status to `Accepted` in readiness to send the quote data to \ncreate a new insurance policy. The TPP must update the status to Accepted before\nretrieving any additional data through their Data Sharing permissions, to include\nin the new insurance policy request.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OzoneConnect.providerId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OzoneConnect.callerOrgId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OzoneConnect.callerClientId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OzoneConnect.callerSoftwareStatementId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OzoneConnect.apiUri"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OzoneConnect.apiOperation"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OzoneConnect.callerInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OzoneConnect.ozoneInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AEInsurance.QuoteId"
        }
      ],
      "responses": {
        "200": {
          "description": "The request has succeeded.",
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "data": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "PolicyIssuanceAllowed": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "CustomerVerification": {
                            "type": "boolean",
                            "description": "Broker allowed to complete capture of customer verification information and documents for this quote."
                          },
                          "Payment": {
                            "type": "boolean",
                            "description": "Broker allowed to host payment checkout."
                          },
                          "PolicyDocuments": {
                            "type": "boolean",
                            "description": "Broker allowed to provide policy documents to customer."
                          }
                        },
                        "required": [
                          "CustomerVerification",
                          "Payment",
                          "PolicyDocuments"
                        ],
                        "description": "Broker requests to handle following steps of policy issuance process."
                      }
                    },
                    "minProperties": 1,
                    "description": "This response **MUST** only be used where there are instruction for TPP acting as a Broker. Please use a `204` response if Broker instructions are not required."
                  },
                  "links": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "PaymentUrl": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "format": "uri",
                        "description": "Hosted payment URL for TPP to present to customer.  Required when the Payment field is true."
                      }
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "PaymentUrl"
                    ],
                    "description": "Links to other resources. Can be omitted where `PaymentUrl` is not returned."
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "data"
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "204": {
          "description": "No content"
        },
        "400": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/error400Response"
        },
        "403": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/error403Response"
        },
        "409": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/error409Response"
        },
        "500": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/error500Response"
        },
        "default": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/errorResponse"
        }
      },
      "tags": [
        "Health Insurance"
      ],
      "requestBody": {
        "required": true,
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "data": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEInsurance.AEHealthInsuranceQuoteAcceptQuoteRequestProperties"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "data"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "security": [
    {},
    {
      "OzoneConnectApiKey": []
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": [
        "placeholder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "securitySchemes": {
    "OzoneConnectApiKey": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using an API Key, which is a secret shared between the API Hub and the LFI.",
      "type": "apiKey",
      "in": "header",
      "name": "Authorization"
    },
    "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": {
      "type": "oauth2",
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using a Client Credentials grant type.\n\nLFIs must host an OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server to utilise this security pattern. Scope values are set during the onboarding process, and represented by a placeholder in this API description.\n",
      "flows": {
        "clientCredentials": {
          "tokenUrl": "https://example.lfi.ae/token",
          "scopes": {
            "placeholder": "Placeholder for scopes, which are set by the LFI during onboarding"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using the \"JWT Auth\" mechanism, where the Client presents a signed JSON Web Token as a credential.\n\nThe Server MUST verify the signature in order to authenticate the Client.\n\nPlease note that the value of the `scheme` parameter is not a registered HTTP Authentication Scheme, to indicate it is specific to Ozone Connect. Please refer to API Hub documentation for further details.\n",
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "Ozone-Connect-JWT-Auth"
    },
    "OzoneConnectServiceInitiationToken": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using a Service Initiation Token.\n\nThe API Hub will set an Access Token based on a value set by the LFI, which has been patched onto the associated consent. The value will be transmitted in the `Authorization` header, which is represented as a `Bearer` in this Security Scheme Object.\n",
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "Bearer"
    }
  }
}

